meta {
  name: 41 - Labels Incremental Sweep
  type: graphql
  seq: 41
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query LabelsIncrementalSweep {
    narrowed: issueLabels(
      first: 250
      includeArchived: true
      orderBy: updatedAt
      filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"}}
    ) {
      nodes { id name updatedAt }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
    }
    wideOpen: issueLabels(
      first: 250
      includeArchived: true
      orderBy: updatedAt
      filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"}}
    ) {
      nodes { id name updatedAt }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/filtering

  The exact incremental query the connector will issue for Labels. Note it uses
  `orderBy: updatedAt` (descending) rather than `sort`, because `issueLabels` rejects the
  `sort` argument — see `42 - Labels Sort Rejected`.

  **Limitation / observed finding** (confirmed 2026-07-30): `IssueLabelFilter.updatedAt`
  IS honored, and this is the one cluster stream besides Issues where narrowing was
  actually demonstrated on live data.

  - `narrowed` (`gt: 2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z`, the exact shared bulk-seed timestamp)
    -> **0 rows**
  - `wideOpen` (`gt: 2020-01-01T00:00:00Z`)
    -> **3 rows** (Bug, Feature, Improvement), `hasNextPage: false`

  3 -> 0 on a 1 ms-exclusive boundary, mirroring `07 - Cursor Filter Boundary` on Issues.
  The `gt` comparator is strictly exclusive here too.

  The `narrowed` alias also re-demonstrates the tie hazard on this stream specifically: all
  3 labels share one `updatedAt`, so a cursor checkpointed at that value excludes the
  entire population. Because Labels sweeps DESCENDING and can only checkpoint at
  end-of-sweep, a partially-completed sweep must NOT advance the cursor at all.
}

example {
  name: 200 — updatedAt filter narrows 3 -> 0 at exact boundary

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query LabelsIncrementalSweep {
        narrowed: issueLabels(
          first: 250
          includeArchived: true
          orderBy: updatedAt
          filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"}}
        ) {
          nodes { id name updatedAt }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        }
        wideOpen: issueLabels(
          first: 250
          includeArchived: true
          orderBy: updatedAt
          filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"}}
        ) {
          nodes { id name updatedAt }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 1250
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2480
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2997750
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "narrowed": {
              "count": 0,
              "rows": []
            },
            "wideOpen": {
              "count": 3,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "Bug",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "Feature",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "Improvement",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
